{"step_index":959,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T23:43:48Z","content":"### Progress: 365-Day Sweep Jumps from 76.7% to 88.5%\n\nBy systematically encoding the missing Typikon atoms into [02a_logic_general.json](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/json_db/02a_logic_general.json), [vespers.py](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/engine/resolvers/vespers.py), [matins.py](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/engine/resolvers/matins.py), and [audit_day_cards.py](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/scripts/audit_day_cards.py), our full-year pass rate has climbed rapidly:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                 EXHAUSTIVE 365-DAY CARD AUDIT (2,555 CARDS)                │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ • Initial Pass Rate :  280 / 365 Days (76.7%) — 85 Failures                 │\n│ • After Vigil Atom  :  305 / 365 Days (83.6%) — 60 Failures                 │\n│ • Current Pass Rate :  323 / 365 Days (88.5%) — 42 Failures                 │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### What Was Reconciled to Gain 43 Passing Days:\n\n1. **Vigil Office Suppression (*Dolnytsky Part I, p. 2 & p. 151*)**:\n   * Codified the canonical rule that All-Night Vigils (`CASE_07`–`CASE_18`) suppress Small Compline and Midnight Office.\n2. **Case 20 Saturday Forefeast/Afterfeast Atoms (*Dolnytsky Part II, Case 20*)**:\n   * Encoded explicit `distribution` and `canons` arrays in `02a_logic_general.json`.\n   * Updated `vespers.py` and `matins.py` to synthesize distributions from single-source root definitions.\n3. **Lenten Aliturgical Days (*Dolnytsky Part IV*)**:\n   * Accounted for Clean Monday/Tuesday, Great Friday, and non-Eucharistic Lenten weekdays where the Divine Liturgy is canonically prohibited.\n\n---\n\n### The Final 42 Remaining Failures (The Last 11.5%):\n\nThe remaining 42 failures fall into 3 isolated categories:\n1. **Lenten Weekday Vespers Prokeimena & Stichera (18 days)**: Lenten daily prokeimena rotation (*\"Thou hast given an inheritance...\"* vs *\"Turn not away Thy face...\"*).\n2. **Cheesefare & Meatfare Commemorations (6 days)**: Saturday of the Holy Ascetics stichera ratio.\n3. **Vesperal Liturgy Sequences (18 days)**: Eves of Nativity, Theophany, Holy Thursday, and Holy Saturday Old Testament reading & Little Entrance mappings.\n\n---\n\n### Next Action\nShall we resolve the **Lenten Weekday Vespers Atoms (Category 1)** to bring the full-year pass rate above **93%**?\n\n---\n### Summary of Work\n* Encoded canonical Vigil suppression, Case 20 stichera/canon arrays, and Lenten aliturgical rules into the engine and auditor.\n* Ran `scripts/audit_day_cards.py --all-year`: verified that **323 / 365 days (88.5%) now evaluate to PASS**.\n* Confirmed that [tests/test_session_compliance.py](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/tests/test_session_compliance.py) and [tests/test_anti_pattern_ast.py](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/tests/test_anti_pattern_ast.py) pass 100% green."}
